Use the global overlay elevation hierarchy.

Do not create giant shadows.

Do not use decorative blur simply because the component floats.

If translucency is used, maintain readability and contrast.

Do not rely on backdrop blur to distinguish surfaces.

Every overlay must maintain clear visual separation from the underlying interface.

Focus management is mandatory.

When a modal overlay opens:
move focus appropriately.

When it closes:
restore focus to the triggering element where appropriate.

Do not trap focus in non-modal overlays.

Modal surfaces must appropriately manage focus.

Escape should close dismissible overlays where appropriate.

Do not allow Escape to bypass a critical confirmation unintentionally.

Click/tap outside behavior must be configurable.

Do not automatically close every overlay when the user clicks outside.

For destructive or critical dialogs:
explicit action should be required.

Prevent background interaction when a modal overlay is active.

Do not allow background content to remain accidentally interactive beneath a modal.

Support nested overlay scenarios carefully.

Avoid uncontrolled overlay stacking.

Overlay z-index values must come from a centralized system.

Never invent arbitrary z-index values per component.

Do not create a separate stacking system for each overlay.

Animations must be short, subtle, and spatially meaningful.

Respect reduced-motion preferences.

Avoid:
bounce
overshoot
large scaling
dramatic zooming
continuous animation

The interface should feel:
stable,
quiet,
precise,
premium,
focused,
and predictable.

Overlay dimensions must be responsive.

Never hardcode desktop dimensions as the only behavior.

Long content must scroll inside the appropriate surface without preventing access to:
close controls
primary actions
critical information

On mobile:
account for:
safe areas
virtual keyboard
orientation
touch targets
system gestures

Do not allow the keyboard to cover important dialog controls.

All overlay content must remain usable at high zoom and dynamic text sizes.

Test:
short content
long content
many actions
long labels
localized content
RTL
keyboard-only interaction
screen readers
touch
high contrast
dark mode
light mode
reduced motion
narrow mobile
wide desktop

No overlay may cause permanent layout corruption after opening or closing.
